The model should use dimensions to filter the relevant fact tables. DimCustomer, DimEnterprise, and DimProduct connect to FactContract using their respective keys; they can also connect to FactContractSnapshot when the snapshot data contains the same dimension keys or can be reliably associated with them. DimDate connects to the applicable contract and snapshot date keys. This structure supports consistent portfolio analysis while keeping contract-level values separate from date-dependent exposure.

Technical note: A star schema should not contain direct fact-to-fact relationships. If the snapshot fact stores only business identifiers, resolve the relevant dimension keys during Snowflake preparation or in a controlled transformation step. Also, attributes such as customer risk band or credit score may change over time; decide whether reports need current values or historically accurate values before placing these attributes in a dimension.
